// BUG REPRO (minimal): owned value moved into a call in `if`-condition
// position double-frees when the condition is FALSE.
// - `is_hi("yo")`: callee takes ownership of the String and frees it;
//   the caller's scope-exit free fires again because the generated
//   null-after-move lands only inside the taken (`true`) branch.
// - ASan (build: gcc -fsanitize=address on target/valvet/m24.c) reports:
//     double-free in vstr_free, first free in callee (find_header),
//     second free in caller (count_merged) at the unconditional
//     scope-exit free; allocation was the caller's vstr_clone.
// - Polarity: condition TRUE runs clean; condition FALSE aborts.
// - Workaround used in papers/shape_infer.valvet: hoist every call that
//   moves an owned argument out of `if` conditions into a preceding
//   `val` binding statement, then test the bound Copy result.
// Repro: ./target/debug/valvet run papers/bug_cond_move.valvet
// Expected: b\ndone ; Actual: free(): double free detected in tcache 2
fun is_hi(s: String): Bool {
    s == "hi"
}

fun main() {
    if (is_hi("yo")) {
        println("a")
    } else {
        println("b")
    }
    println("done")
}
